  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## v1.9.0 — Multi-targeting .NET 10 and .NET 11\n\n**100% backwards compatible** — the public API surface, defaults, presets and configuration paths are unchanged. The package now ships a `net11.0` asset next to the existing `net10.0` one, so a .NET 11 application resolves the build made for its runtime instead of falling back to `net10.0`.\n\n**What's new:**\n- `lib/net11.0` — the same public API, compiled against .NET 11 (C# 15 and the .NET 11 JIT). `lib/net10.0` is unchanged and stays the target for .NET 10 applications.\n- C# 15 collection-expression arguments (`[with(capacity: ...)]`, `[with(comparer: ...)]`) where the capacity or comparer is known, so the diagnostics preview no longer grows its header map and the options validator passes its comparer inside the collection expression. No behavior change.\n- Repository: publishing is keyless through nuget.org trusted publishing, and mutation testing with Stryker.NET records the test-suite baseline in `docs/development/mutation-testing.md`.\n\nSee CHANGELOG.md and docs/ for full details.",
